      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- TIP_DETAIL\n- SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n\n## Column Mapping\n- department name: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- average enrollment: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- enrollment variance: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- average total units: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\n- variance of total units: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\n- Chemistry: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- material record: TIP_DETAIL.RECORD_COUNT\n- degree-granting departments: SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- Biology: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- 2022 academic year: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n\n## Join Keys\n- TIP_DETAIL.TERM_CODE <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n\n## Domain Knowledge\n- \"Chemistry\" is predicated by \"TABLE.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Chemistry'\"\n- \"degree-granting\" is predicated by \"TABLE.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'\"\n- \"Course 5\" is predicated by \"TABLE.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Chemistry'\"\n- \"Biology\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_CODE = '7'\"\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each department, provide the department name and calculate the average and variance of the number of enrolled students in courses that have at least one associated material record, but only include courses from the Chemistry department (Course 5).\n```sql\nSELECT tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, AVG(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS avg_enrollment, VARIANCE(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrollment_variance FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso JOIN TIP_DETAIL td ON tso.TERM_CODE = td.TERM_CODE WHERE td.RECORD_COUNT > 0 AND tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Chemistry' GROUP BY tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME ORDER BY enrollment_variance DESC;\n```\n2. For each department, provide the department name and calculate the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2022 academic year, but only include departments that grant degrees and exclude the Biology department (Course 7).\n```sql\nSELECT sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, AVG(ccso.TOTAL_UNITS) AS avg_total_units, VARIANCE(ccso.TOTAL_UNITS) AS var_total_units FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT sd JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ccso ON sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = ccso.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE sd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND ccso.ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2022 AND sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '7' GROUP BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME ;\n```\n\n## Question\nList, for each department, the department name, the average and variance of the number of enrolled students in Chemistry courses with at least one associated material record, and the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered by degree-granting departments (excluding Biology) in the 2022 academic year. For each row, indicate the reason for inclusion as either 'ChemistryEnrollment' or 'DegreeDeptUnits'. The columns should be: department name, average enrollment, enrollment variance, average total units, variance of total units, and reason for inclusion, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers."
